Map of this area: `docs/map/frontend.md` - read it before searching for a file.

## Structure

Next.js 15, App Router, TypeScript, feature-first.

- `app/<feature>/page.tsx` - one folder per route.
- `components/<Name>.tsx` - shared components, created only once something is reused twice.
- `lib/api-client.ts` - one API client. Not `fetch` scattered across components.

Don't create empty folders ahead of need.

## Rules

- **All user-facing text is Polish.** Identifiers, comments, and file names are English. Never mix the two inside one artifact.
- `strict: true` stays on. No `any` without a comment explaining why.
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when the component actually needs interactivity or browser APIs.
- API base URL comes from `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. It is read by the browser, so it must be host-reachable - never the Docker service name.
- `PascalCase` for components (file and symbol), `camelCase` for functions and variables, `kebab-case` for non-component files.
- No component library, state manager, or styling framework is installed. Adding one is a recorded decision in `docs/architecture.md`, not a drive-by `npm install`.
- Past ~300 lines or doing two things → split the file, and update the map row.

## Running it

Everything runs in Docker. `package.json` changes need a rebuild (`docker compose up -d --build frontend`), not a restart.
